{"type": "thinking", "text": "Same: no visual indicator of current selection (Spanish). Hmm. Is this normal AnkiDroid behavior? Let me recall... In AnkiDroid 2.17 note editor, tapping Deck opens \"Select a deck\" dialog. I believe the currently selected deck has a checkmark on the left of its row. Actually I remember the deck picker dialog in AnkiDroid: DeckPickerDialog lists decks in a list; the selected deck's name appears in blue/green? Hmm.\n\nActually, AnkiDroid's `DeckSelectionDialog.kt` uses `DeckAdapter` and `DeckItem` view with `deck_name` and `deck_counts`, and there's a checkmark shown for the selected deck: I recall `updateDeckSelection` sets `deckName.autoSizeTextType`... not enough.\n\nConsider the actual Anki Desktop deck chooser—it has a checkmark. AnkiDroid 2.16 deck chooser (when you tap the deck name in the toolbar of Add note) I'm fairly sure shows a checkmark on the currently selected deck. Let me see if maybe the indicator only shows after rotation? no.\n\nAnother way: the bug might be that the checkmark is missing because the initial selection is not being set (i.e., adapter's selectedDeckId isn't set) — that fits the \"initial deck loaded from deck list's current choice\" change: maybe the code was changed to use deck list's current choice, and the selection isn't marked. Hmm, but the developer says \"initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice\" — the change itself. The seeded bug could be that this initial deck is wrong (e.g., uses deck list's default \"1\" deck id or stale choice), which manifests as no check highlighted... but there is no highlight at all, so can't tell.\n\nWait: maybe the \"deck chooser\" is not this dialog but the note editor's deck spinner? Hmm no.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the deck chooser selection is indicated by text color — selected deck in blue. In screenshot both black. So none selected.\n\nLet me test: If selection is functional, tapping the first row French selects French. If the dialog had initial selection Spanish, then tapping Cancel then reopening would show... no indicator.\n\nMaybe the intended check: after choosing a deck in the Add screen, going back to deck list, the deck list's *current* deck changes? Hmm.\n\nLet me think about AnkiDroid code. In `NoteEditor`, field `mCurrentDid` (current deck id). On add: if intent has deck id, use it; else `ColHelper.getCurrentDeckId`? Actually the change \"Add note deck chooser: its initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice\" suggests a code path like `DeckSelectionDialog.show(... currentDeckId = ...)` where the dialog is also a launcher for adding a note from the deck picker. Hmm, \"Add note deck chooser\" could be a dialog shown when pressing + FAB: maybe there's a deck chooser dialog that appears before the note editor when multiple decks? No.\n\nHold on. In newer AnkiDroid (2.15+), pressing the \"+\" FAB in the deck picker opens a quickly-launched note editor using \"current deck\". The menu item \"Add note\" in deck long-press passes deck id. If no current deck, first deck.\n\nMaybe the actual changed screen: when adding a note (from anywhere), the note editor's deck chooser (the deck field dialog) initially shows the deck list's current choice (not the note editor's current deck). A seeded bug could be: after choosing deck French in note editor, opening the chooser again still highlights Spanish (deck list current), and if you tap Cancel nothing changes; if you tap a deck... Hmm.\n\nBut without a selection indicator, how would QA detect? Maybe the selection indicator does exist as a checkmark but only when `selectedDeckId` matches; since it's missing for both French and Spanish, maybe the dialog receives \"-1\" selection → bug \"initial deck not shown\". This is a plausible seeded bug: \"deck chooser initial deck loaded from deck list's current choice\" — if collection's current deck is Spanish, checkmark should be on Spanish. It's absent → bug.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the dialog shows a radio/check only in \"Deck picker\" when opened from deck list? Let me verify with the known-good state: In AnkiDroid 2.17.0, adding a note: tap \"Deck\" → dialog \"Select a deck\" with deck names and counts? I'm quite sure the selected deck has a checkmark (the same dialog style as \"Select tags\" with checkboxes!). The \"Select tags\" dialog uses checkboxes. The deck dialog in this build shows no checkboxes at all. That strongly suggests a missing selection indicator (checkbox/check) — likely the seeded bug.\n\nBut hmm, is a checkbox shown for decks in stock AnkiDroid? The dialog in stock: I found memory of \"DeckSelectionDialog\" with `deck_selection_dialog.xml` and item `deck_item.xml` including `deck_name` and `deck_counts` and a `checkmark`? There is a `deck_checkmark` ImageView... I believe yes: AnkiDroid's deck selection dialog shows a checkmark for currently selected deck. Let me search my memory of AnkiDroid strings: `deck_selection_dialog_title_select_deck`. The adapter `DeckAdapter` has `notifyDataSetChanged`, and in `onBindViewHolder`: `holder.mDeckName.setText(...)`, `holder.mCheckMark.setVisibility(deck.isSelected ? VISIBLE : GONE)`? I have moderate confidence.\n\nActually I recall AnkiDroid uses `DeckPickerItem` with checkmark when a deck is selected in \"study options\"/deck chooser. In the \"Add note\" deck chooser, I think it's a simple list without checkmarks... Hmm.\n\nLet me test the functionality differently: Does the dialog remember/apply the note editor's current deck? I could use \"Select all/cancel\" trick: If I tap the initial-selected deck, the editor should retain same deck. That works regardless.\n\nCould there be an \"unselected\" bug where tapping Cancel changes deck? Let's test cancel: tap Cancel now, verify Deck still Spanish."}
