{"type": "thinking", "text": "Deleted temp subdeck, Spanish arrow gone (no deck_expander in tree). Good — arrow removal works.\n\nNow the deck list area looks fine. Let me test more: deck list counts after adding note (from old tests) matched. Also check \"Browse cards\" from a deck long-press opens browser for that deck? That's navigation consistency. Let me test that quickly later.\n\nNext: card browser tag dialog refresh more thoroughly. Test case: add a tag via browser's \"Edit tags\" (set tags dialog on selected cards), then reopen Filter by tag dialog — should include it. Also test deleting a tag: remove tag from note via edit tags, then reopen the dialog — if the tag no longer exists in collection (unused tag may persist). Actually AnkiDroid's tag list likely includes unused tags... The changed behavior \"tag list refreshed from the collection each time the dialog opens\" implies previously stale. Our first test showed refresh works.\n\nBut wait — there might be a seeded bug related: for example, the tag dialog list not refreshing when opened the second time after adding a tag in note editor. Our test passed. Maybe the bug relates to deleting tags: e.g., tag list showing deleted/unused tags? Hmm.\n\nActually let's be careful: our test added testtag and saw it. We then deleted the note but testtag persists in collection tags. That's normal.\n\nMaybe the seeded bug is elsewhere, e.g., the tag dialog's \"filter tags\" search or select state. Or the dialog might show a stale count. Hmm.\n\nLet me test adding a tag through the browser's \"Edit tags\" dialog, which is a different dialog (tags dialog for selected notes). After adding, reopen tag filter dialog → tag appears. That works likely.\n\nPotential seeded bug: when you add a tag in browser via Edit tags and then reopen the tag filter dialog, the list might show stale?? Our note-editor test already triggers collection tag change; dialog refreshed.\n\nLet's think about the three changed items and what bugs could be seeded:\n1. Deck list arrows only for decks with subdecks — we saw correct behavior with Spanish::temp (arrow shown) and removed (arrow gone). French no arrow. Seems fine. But maybe bug: arrow shown for decks that contain subdecks but empty parents? Or the subdeck row itself (temp, which has no subdecks) gets no arrow — correct. Maybe a deck with subdecks collapsed vs expanded state persisted? Rotation? Could test rotation with expanded.\n\n2. Add note deck chooser initial deck from deck list current choice — untested properly.\n\n3. Browser tag dialog refresh — seemed to work.\n\nLet me scrutinize #2. How does the deck list \"current choice\" manifest? The deck list row doesn't show a \"current deck\" marker unless you select? In AnkiDroid, tapping a deck opens the study screen, setting it as current; the deck list header says \"AnkiDroid\" not deck name. Hmm, but there's a setting \"Deck list: current deck\"? Actually the current deck is used when you press the + FAB; it's the deck you last studied/opened.\n\nTest procedure:\n- Tap French deck row → opens deck overview (\"Study\" screen for French) → back to deck list. Now current deck = French presumably.\n- Press + FAB \"Add\" → note editor should open Deck: French.\n- Open deck chooser in Add screen → initial deck should be French (deck list's current choice?). Hmm but the note editor's deck is French too.\n\nWait, here's the subtle scenario in the changed item: \"Add note deck chooser: its initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice.\" Perhaps when you open the Add screen, the deck shown is loaded from the deck list's current choice. That's the \"deck chooser\" = the deck field/spinner? Hmm, \"chooser\" suggests the dialog.\n\nAlternatively maybe the \"Add note deck chooser\" is a dialog that appears when pressing + from deck list if \"Deck selection\" setting? Hmm.\n\nLet me test the actual behavior:\n1. From deck list, tap French (goes to study screen). Press BACK. Current deck now French?\n2. Tap + FAB → check Deck.\nIf Deck shows French → matches \"deck list's current choice\".\nThen open deck chooser → check (no indicator though) selection by... hmm.\n\nLet me also test when deck list current choice differs from note editor deck: In Add screen choose deck Spanish via chooser, then press Back (discard), go back to deck list (current choice French), press + again → Deck should be French (not Spanish) if it loads from deck list current choice. If it shows Spanish, that's a bug (it retained the editor's last deck instead of deck list current). That's a plausible seeded bug! The changed behavior: initial deck from deck list's current choice (not last-used in note editor). Hmm, but the note editor's deck persists per session? AnkiDroid remembers last deck used for adding notes? Actually in AnkiDroid, new note deck defaults to the current deck in deck picker; the note editor state is per-launch.\n\nLet me test: current deck French vs. Add deck Spanish.\n\nFirst, exit browser back to deck list. Currently we're at deck list already. Tap French deck row (7) to set current deck French? That opens study screen. Let's do it, then back."}
