{"type": "thinking", "text": "Add screen shows Deck: French — matches deck list current choice (French). Good.\n\nNow the deck chooser dialog initial deck: the current deck is French. If the dialog highlights nothing, maybe the bug. Let's test scenario where editor deck changed: In this Add screen, choose Spanish via chooser. Then leave Add (discard or back with empty fields), return deck list (current French), press + again → editor deck French. That tests initial deck from deck list choice.\n\nBut also, the deck chooser's initial selection: supposed to be loaded from deck list's current choice. If the deck chooser in a Spanish-selected editor still highlights French... no indicator.\n\nMaybe there's an alternative: the deck chooser dialog could list decks with counts. Hmm, only names.\n\nWait, maybe I'm wrong about the checkmark. Let me check what AnkiDroid 2.17 deck selection dialog looks like. From source memory (AnkiDroid `DeckSelectionDialog.kt`): It uses `DeckAdapter` with `Deck` list; each item layout `deck_selection_dialog_item.xml`? Hmm. I recall a dialog where current deck is shown with a checkmark at the left, and deck names are indented for subdecks. Actually I think that's the \"deck picker\" in the study options? In AnkiDroid 2.16, when tapping the deck name on the Add note screen, you get \"Select a deck\" dialog listing decks, and the currently selected deck has a checkmark to the right. Yes, I'm fairly sure — the dialog uses `R.layout.deck_item` with a `CheckBox`? Hmm.\n\nLet me compare with the tag dialog: tag dialog has actual checkboxes. The deck dialog items were LinearLayout \"DeckPickerHoriz\" (horizontal recycler view item). Could be from `DeckPickerItem` layout used in a horizontal recycler? Hmm no.\n\nI want more evidence. Let's test the dialog in a state where the note editor's deck is Spanish but the deck list current is French, then see if any deck appears selected. If the selection is invisible always, can't distinguish. Maybe the selection is shown by bold font or background? Screenshot showed both normal.\n\nAlternatively, examine the JSON via accessibility: observe shows \"contains French\" and \"contains Spanish\" with no \"checked\" or \"selected\" flags. For the tags dialog, checkboxes show `CheckBox id=check_box_view [clickable]` without checked state either (even when checked!). In screenshot, testtag checkbox was checked, but observe didn't say checked. Hmm, observe does label RadioButton checked state (\"All cards [clickable,checked]\"), but the CheckBox showed no checked attribute in the list even when checked visually. So observe may omit checked for checkbox. Not reliable.\n\nSo the deck dialog might have a checkmark image that observe doesn't expose (image with no content desc). But screenshot clearly shows no checkmark on either row. Unless the checkmark is a subtle icon... In the screenshot, the rows are just text, no icon at left or right. So no selection indicator. For the tag dialog, checkboxes visible on right. For deck dialog, nothing.\n\nLet me check stock AnkiDroid: maybe the deck dialog uses radio buttons? Hmm.\n\nIs a missing checkmark a bug worth reporting? The changed feature says \"initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice\". Perhaps the seeded defect is that the initial deck is not indicated AND when you tap \"Cancel\" ... no effect.\n\nWait, maybe I can detect initial selection by the behavior of the \"Filter decks\" search? No.\n\nDifferent idea: perhaps the deck chooser's \"initial deck\" determines which deck gets selected when using the \"Add\" (+) button in the dialog... no, + creates a deck.\n\nMaybe the note editor's deck chooser initial deck affects the list scroll position (current deck scrolled into view). With only 2 decks, both visible.\n\nHmm. What if the bug is about the \"Deck:\" label on the Add screen not being loaded from deck list's current choice (e.g., always Spanish because \"current deck\" wasn't updated)? But we saw French correctly.\n\nLet me test another route: The deck list long-press → \"Add\" for Spanish (we did at the start) opened Add with Deck: Spanish. Good.\n\nLet me test: while in Add with deck Spanish (chosen via chooser), press Back (empty fields) → deck list; press + FAB → deck French (current choice). If it shows Spanish instead → bug (initial deck not from deck list current choice, but last note-editor choice). Let's test.\n\nOpen chooser, select Spanish."}
