{"type": "thinking", "text": "Whoa! The FAB bubble still shows French even after I opened Spanish deck and backed out. Hmm! Tapping the Spanish deck row opens the study screen (deck overview?) with \"comer\" — wait, tapping deck row in AnkiDroid goes straight to study (or deck overview). The \"current deck\" should become Spanish. But bubble shows French. That's a potential bug! Let me think.\n\nWhen tapping a deck row, it becomes the current deck. Earlier, tapping French updated the bubble to French (before it was presumably... hmm, initially maybe bubble was French already? Actually we never saw the bubble initially; the app starts with current deck = first? Let me recall: the initial deck list + FAB bubble? We didn't open FAB before tapping French. Hmm: First FAB expansion happened after tapping French → bubble French. So the current deck might have been French all along (default current deck set by last-used). Then tapping Spanish should change bubble to Spanish, but it shows French. Suspicious!\n\nBut wait: tapping Spanish deck opens the study screen with comer. Then pressing BACK returns to deck picker. Maybe the deck picker's \"current deck\" isn't updated by simply opening? In AnkiDroid, tapping a deck sets it as current deck (the \"current deck\" is used as default for adding notes). Actually the deck picker's `selectDeck` sets `mCurrentDeckId`... Hmm. In older AnkiDroid, opening a deck sets the \"current deck\" and the menu says \"Decks\" with current highlighted. The + button adds to current deck.\n\nMaybe pressing BACK during study because of \"Press back twice to go back/exit\" setting! Remember \"Press back twice to go back/exit\" is enabled by default? The setting says \"To avoid accidentally leaving the study screen or the app\". If enabled, pressing back once shows a toast \"Press back again to exit\" and stays; second press exits. Our single BACK returned to deck list though. Hmm, maybe the setting is off.\n\nBut the bubble showing French after studying Spanish suggests current deck didn't update. Alternatively, the FAB bubble shows the *last deck used to add notes* or the \"current deck\" from a stored preference that updates only when... hmm.\n\nLet's verify: Maybe the bubble shows the deck of the last added note? We last added browertest in Spanish, but bubble shows French. Hmm no.\n\nActually the current deck in AnkiDroid is stored in collection config `curDeck`. Opening a deck to study sets curDeck = that deck id. When returning, deck picker reads curDeck? The bubble view is created when FAB expands, reading curDeck. It shows French... Maybe our BACK from the study screen didn't save because we didn't answer any card? No, selecting deck is enough usually.\n\nHmm wait, maybe tapping a deck row opens the \"deck overview\" screen (with Study button) rather than study directly — but we saw a flashcard with \"comer\" and \"Show answer\", i.e., study screen directly. In AnkiDroid 2.17 tapping a deck opens study directly (new study screen?). The current deck is set.\n\nLet me test again carefully: go back to deck list (press back maybe from this expanded FAB first). Then tap Spanish, wait, back, expand FAB, check bubble.\n\nActually we're in the FAB expanded menu. Tap Add? No, first let's close FAB (tap bubble? or back). Let me press BACK."}
