{"type": "thinking", "text": "Let me tap Spanish again and back and then check bubble. But is Spanish deck \"current\" indicated anywhere else? The deck list maybe highlights the current deck with a different background? Looking at screenshots: French row and Spanish row look same (white). Hmm, in AnkiDroid deck picker, the current deck is not highlighted.\n\nMaybe the current deck only changes when you actually study a card? Let's test by studying a Spanish card: tap Spanish, then \"Show answer\", then rate \"Good\"? That would change review stats (undesirable but minor; it's the study data, not part of our areas). Better not.\n\nAlternatively, in this AnkiDroid version, the FAB bubble displays the current deck based on preference updated by the deck picker each time you open the app? Hmm.\n\nLet me look at that from the \"changed\" perspective: \"Add note deck chooser: its initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice.\" Hmm, maybe the intended change is the opposite direction? \"the deck list's current choice\" could refer to the deck selected in the Deck Picker screen (mCurrentDeckId). The bug could be that the deck list's current choice is not updated when tapping a deck (so initial deck stale = French). But our Add screen did show French while current should be Spanish... That means the \"deck list's current choice\" as seen by the app is French, even after tapping Spanish. But then the app's current choice is wrong vs the user's implied choice (they tapped Spanish).\n\nHmm, but is tapping a deck row supposed to change the \"current deck\" used for adds? In AnkiDroid, I believe yes: the deck picker header shows \"Deck picker\" and the current deck is used for the + button. Actually in AnkiDroid the + FAB \"Add\" always opens the note editor with the deck from the LAST used deck? Let me recall: In AnkiDroid 2.16, there is a setting \"Deck for new cards: Use current deck / Decide by note type\". The current deck is the deck you last opened. So if you open Spanish and back, the new note should go to Spanish. The fact that Add shows French is suspicious.\n\nBut wait: Did tapping Spanish actually open Spanish? The flashcard showed \"comer\" which is Spanish (comer is Spanish, tagged verb). Yes, Spanish. Then back. Bubble French. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the FAB bubble is not \"current deck\" but \"deck to add note to\" from a different source: maybe it's the deck list's \"current deck\" which updates only after answering? Let me test more definitively using the Add screen deck:\n- Tap Spanish → study screen (comer) → answer a card? That changes review state (comer becomes learned). Avoid.\n- After opening Spanish and backing out, tap + → Add. What deck? We did that: Add showed French. Then tap deck chooser and select Spanish, then save a note... The note goes to the chosen deck. Fine.\n\nSo is this \"current deck not updated\" a bug in the changed feature? The changed feature is \"Add note deck chooser: initial deck now loaded from the deck list's current choice\". If the deck list's current choice is French (stale), maybe that's the bug: the current choice isn't updated when selecting Spanish deck. But maybe the deck list's \"current choice\" is intentionally distinct: in AnkiDroid, the current deck changes only when you tap the deck (study), which we did. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at what \"current choice\" means in the DeckPicker: In AnkiDroid source, DeckPicker has `mCurrentDeck`? Hmm. There is \"DeckPicker.currentDeckId\" maybe derived from `col.get_config(\"curDeck\")`. Tapping a deck calls `openStudyOptions`/`onDeckClick` with `updateCurrentDeck = true`? I recall the deck picker stores \"currentDeckId\" in `Preferences` or the collection config when clicking on a deck. Yes: `DeckPicker.onDeckClick` → `openStudyOptions(deckId)`; and `openStudyOptions` sets `getCol().getDecks().select(deckId)`. So it should update.\n\nThen why French? Unless the FAB bubble and Add deck are cached from... Hmm, maybe tapping Spanish deck on the deck picker did NOT actually select Spanish because the app opened study screen via another path that doesn't set current? Weird.\n\nLet me reproduce cleanly:\n1. From deck list, tap Spanish, wait 1s, check study shows comer.\n2. Back.\n3. Tap + (FAB expand) → bubble text. If French again → reproducible.\n\nWe already did exactly that. Result French. Let me also test: restart app? open_app brings foreground, doesn't reset. Hmm. Killing app not possible except force stop (not available). \n\nMaybe the deck picker's current deck is only updated when you press \"Study\" from the deck overview page (not by tapping the row?). The study screen we entered might be because tapping the row starts study directly; the deck picker's `currentDeck` should be set at the moment of the click though.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the FAB bubble shows the *default* deck from the \"deck for new cards\" setting? With \"Decide by note type\" now selected, the bubble might show note type's deck = French! That would explain: The bubble may show the deck that an added note would go to (i.e., the note type's deck). Earlier, before switching the setting, after tapping French the bubble showed French (matching both). Now with \"Decide by note type\", the bubble shows French because Basic's deck is French. Hmm! And the Add screen showed French as well — consistent with \"decide by note type\" and Basic→French. So the setting DID apply, and the note type deck is French! That resolves the apparent inconsistency: the FAB bubble and Add screen reflect the note type's deck (French) because of the setting.\n\nWait but does the FAB bubble depend on the setting? Possibly the FAB's \"Add\" action opens NoteEditor which computes deck by setting; and the bubble label maybe computed likewise (\"will add to French\"). That seems plausible and consistent.\n\nSo to test \"Decide by note type\", we need to know Basic's deck. If Basic's deck is French, then with setting on and current Spanish, Add shows French. That's what we observed. Good, setting works.\n\nNow switch back to \"Use current deck\" and verify Add shows Spanish (current). That tests the setting and current choice. Let's do that: Go to Settings → General → Deck for new cards → Use current deck. Then back to deck list (+ will show bubble?), Add → expect Spanish.\n\nActually careful: the current deck is now Spanish (we opened Spanish). If Add shows Spanish with \"Use current deck\", then the deck list current choice updated correctly. Good, and then the earlier French was due to note type setting. \n\nLet me set the setting back. We are at deck list. Drawer → Settings → General → Deck for new cards → Use current deck."}
