{"type": "thinking", "text": "All decks: 7 cards (4 Spanish + 3 French), matching deck list totals (3+4=7). Good.\n\nNow test the tag dialog in all-decks mode: open filter by tag — tag list should show testtag and verb (collection-wide). Actually earlier in Spanish mode it showed both. Fine.\n\nNow test adding a tag via browser's \"Edit tags\" (tags dialog for selected cards) and then reopening filter-by-tag to check refresh. This is a slightly different path. Let me long-press comer (Spanish note with verb) and use \"Edit tags\". Then add a new tag \"browsertag\", confirm. Then reopen filter dialog → expect browsertag. Then remove the tag from the note (edit tags, uncheck) and maybe the tag remains in collection; also clean up by... hmm, unused tags persist. Deleting the note isn't ideal (comer is precondition data). Adding a tag to comer changes data; can remove tag afterwards (tag will remain unused but note restored). Precondition \"No other tags exist\" would be violated by an unused tag lingering; we already have testtag lingering. Cleanup issue.\n\nAlternative: Use a temporary note (add note with tag) then delete it, as before. The tag remains unused anyway. To remove tags from the collection entirely, AnkiDroid has \"Check database\" which purges unused tags? Let me check Settings → Advanced (maybe under \"Backups\"?). The Settings categories list doesn't show \"Advanced\". Hmm: General, New study screen, Reviewing, Sync, Notifications, Appearance, Controls, Accessibility, Backups, and a partially visible item at 2326. Let me scroll the settings list. There's likely \"Advanced\" at the bottom. The \"Check database\" action is in Deck picker's overflow? The deck picker overflow had \"Check\" (first item). \"Check\" = Check database, maybe \"Check media\"? It likely runs integrity check which may purge unused tags? In Anki, Check Database does remove unused tags? Hmm, I believe \"Check Database\" in Anki desktop removes unused tags only if \"delete unused tags\" option? Not sure. Anki's `col.tags.all()` returns tags from the tags table, and unused tags are only removed when `col.tags.register`... Actually Anki stores tags in `tags` table; deleting notes doesn't delete tags automatically? In Anki desktop, when a tag is no longer used, it disappears from the tag list after \"Check Database\" or after the next sync? Hmm. In Anki 2.1, unused tags are removed when the collection is saved? There's a \"Clear Unused Tags\" in Anki desktop's \"Check Database\"? I recall AnkiDroid has \"Check database\" which \"removes unused tags\"? \n\nLet me just test: deck picker overflow → \"Check\" (element 0). But careful: \"Check\" might mean \"Check media\". The first menu item \"Check\" with items \"Create backup\", \"Restore from backup\", \"Manage note types\", \"Import\", \"Export\". Let me open it to see what it says.\n\nActually before cleanup, continue testing.\n\nBrowser test: search. Tap Search, type \"tag:verb\" (only comer has verb). Verify only comer. Also test \"deck:French\" etc. That's fine.\n\nMore important areas: editing notes via browser, and the tag dialog. Already did.\n\nLet me test note editing edge cases:\n- Empty front field: try saving a note with empty front → should warn \"Front is empty\" / cannot save.\n- Tag dialog cancel: opening Tags, adding a tag then Cancel — should not apply.\n- Deck change in edit mode then save moves card between decks: check deck counts update.\n\nAlso test \"Cards: Card 1\" button? That opens card template. Not needed.\n\n\"Settings that affect them\": We tested \"Deck for new cards\". Another setting: \"Paste clipboard images as PNG\" (editing), unlikely to test. There's \"New study screen\" settings maybe \"Show answer button\"? Not note-related.\n\nMaybe \"Full screen navigation drawer\". Not relevant.\n\nLet me test empty field save. Currently in browser. Tap Add button (2) in browser, then Save with empty fields."}
