{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good: \"The first field is empty.\" snackbar, no note added. \n\nNow test tag dialog Cancel behavior: open Tags, add \"canceltag\" via + → Add, then Cancel in tags dialog (don't confirm). Check \"Tags:\" unchanged. This also tests that adding a tag to collection via + then canceling dialog — does the collection tag get created? In AnkiDroid, \"+\" in tags dialog adds the tag to the note's tag list (and the collection) immediately? The snackbar said \"Touch Confirm to confirm adding testtag\". If you Cancel, does the tag still get added to collection? Probably not (registered on confirm). But the tag may already be registered in the collection when added via dialog \"+\"; hmm. This matters for the tag list refresh — a new tag created but not applied could appear in browser's tag list. Let's test: use + to add \"canceltag\", then Cancel the tags dialog. Then check browser tag list: does \"canceltag\" appear? If yes, is that a bug? The tag was never applied; but AnkiDroid historically registers tags when added in the dialog immediately (the dialog writes tags to note on Confirm only?). Hmm.\n\nThis is a good edge case for \"card browser tag dialog refresh\": if a tag is created but canceled, should the tag list include it? The collection tag is registered when the dialog \"+\" creates it; canceling the note tag selection leaves it as an unused tag in the collection → browser tag list would show it. That's Anki behavior (unused tags remain until check DB). Probably not a reportable bug.\n\nLet's instead focus on testing the reported changed behaviors and general quality of the three areas.\n\nAnother thought: maybe there IS a seeded bug in the tag dialog: the \"Filter by tag\" dialog's tag list should refresh each time it opens; we saw it did for a new tag. But what about a REMOVED tag? Suppose a tag exists in the collection with no notes (unused). It still shows — that's normal-ish. What about tags that were deleted via \"Edit tags\" in browser, i.e., unchecking all tags on a note then confirm? The tag remains but unused; tag list still shows it. Could be considered stale? Hmm no, collection tags include unused.\n\nWhat about adding a tag in the *card browser's Edit tags* dialog? The dialog likely has the same + button; after adding and confirming, reopening filter dialog should show it. That's mostly the same code path as the note editor's dialog. Our test used note editor → filter dialog refresh. Fine.\n\nOK, let me test the browser's \"Edit tags\" dialog for correctness: select comer, Edit tags → checkbox for \"verb\" should be checked (note has verb), testtag unchecked. This is a consistency check. Then cancel.\n\nLet me do it: select comer, overflow → Edit tags."}
