{"type": "thinking", "text": "verb checked, testtag unchecked — correct consistency.\n\nNow cancel. Then test the tag filter dialog using the typed search: open filter by tag, tap \"Filter tags\" (search icon), type \"verb\" → list filters. Also check that the tag dialog refresh still works after cancel etc.\n\nMore valuable: test the tag dialog refresh scenario where a tag is added on a note and then the dialog reopened MULTIPLE times. Already tested once.\n\nHmm, I should look for an actual bug. So far everything works. Maybe I'm missing something in the changed features. Let me re-read:\n\n- \"Card browser tag dialog: the tag list is now refreshed from the collection each time the dialog opens.\" Our test: add note with tag testtag → open filter-by-tag dialog (first time after adding) → shows testtag. Pass.\n\nBut wait: the dialog was previously opened BEFORE adding testtag (we opened it at the start, showing only verb). Then after adding testtag, reopened → showed testtag. This exactly validates refresh. Pass.\n\n- \"Add note deck chooser: its initial deck is now loaded from the deck list's current choice.\" We validated the Add screen's deck = deck list current (Spanish highlighted). But the *chooser dialog* has no selection indicator to validate. Maybe the initial deck is used to order?? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the deck chooser's \"initial deck\" matters when you **change note type**! In the Add note screen, if you change the note type (spinner), the deck may switch to the note type's deck (when \"Decide by note type\"). Not chooser.\n\nAlternatively, the \"deck chooser\" may refer to the dialog in the **deck picker screen for adding a note**: When you tap \"Add\" in deck list FAB? The Add button directly opens note editor. Hmm.\n\nOr maybe it refers to the \"Select a deck\" dialog shown when you press the overflow \"Add note\" from the deck list when multiple decks? No.\n\nLet me look at the note editor's More options menu — maybe there's \"Deck\" option there? No.\n\nCould the \"deck chooser\" be the \"Deck:\" spinner in the note editor? Tap it opens the dialog. The initial deck = deck list's current choice. When adding a note from a deck (long-press → Add), the initial deck should be that deck? We tested long-press Spanish → Add showed Spanish, but that's the note's deck, not chooser.\n\nHmm, let me test a scenario for the chooser's initial deck that's observable: In the Add screen with deck list current = Spanish but note editor deck changed to French via chooser. Then open the chooser again. If \"initial deck\" = deck list current choice (Spanish) rather than editor's current deck (French), then... any observable? Pressing Cancel → no. Selecting \"some\" — no.\n\nUnless the dialog's initial selection affects double-tap behavior: In AnkiDroid's deck dialog, tapping a deck selects it immediately (as we saw). No.\n\nCould the initial deck affect the deck list ordering (current deck scrolled to top)? With 2 decks no.\n\nMaybe the initial deck is used when the user presses \"Add\" (+) in the dialog with a name equal to... no.\n\nI think the initial deck is simply the selection highlighted... but this build's dialog doesn't show a highlighted item at all. Hmm, but maybe it does and I can't see it because the selected item is Spanish whose row is below... Let me re-open the chooser with a 3-deck scenario to compare rows/ordering? We can create a third deck, then the selected deck (Spanish) would be between French and temp; still no visual.\n\nLet me look at the deck dialog fonts more carefully via screenshot pixel positions. Both rows \"French\" and \"Spanish\" start at x=176. If selected had a checkmark at left (x~100), we'd see it. Nothing.\n\nMaybe the selection indicator is a *background color* on the selected row. In the first deck chooser screenshot, both rows appear light blue (#eef4f8-ish). Let me compare with the tag dialog: rows white? In tag dialog screenshot, the dialog background is very light blue and rows have no distinct color; checkboxes at right. In deck dialog, the two rows separated by lines, same background. If selected row were highlighted, we'd likely see a distinct tint. Not present.\n\nI lean towards \"no selection indicator by design\" (AnkiDroid's DeckSelectionDialog may indeed not mark selection; it's destructive selection). Let me verify via the browser deck dialog too: current \"Spanish\" (browser filtered to Spanish), dialog shows All decks/French/Spanish with no marks. So consistent across dialogs; likely stock behavior. Not a bug.\n\nOK, so maybe the seeded bug is more subtle and functional. Let's test the tag dialog refresh more adversarially:\n\nScenario: Open browser tag dialog, leave it open? No, it's modal. Open dialog, cancel, add tag via another route, reopen → done.\n\nScenario: Two tags: add tag with mixed case? Tags are case-sensitive-ish? \"Verb\" vs \"verb\" may be normalized. Not our area.\n\nScenario: Delete a note carrying a tag and then reopen the dialog: tag remains (unused). Not bug.\n\nScenario: Rename a tag? There is no rename.\n\nScenario: The tag list should be refreshed \"from the collection\" — perhaps the bug is that the dialog doesn't show newly added tags if it was opened previously *in the same browser session* and the collection changed externally? We did exactly that and it worked.\n\nHmm, maybe the seeded bug is in the *deck list arrows*, subtle: \"arrows are now built only for decks that contain subdecks\". We saw correct behavior. But what about a deck with subdecks that is itself a subdeck? E.g., Spanish::temp with sub-subdeck Spanish::temp::x. The parent temp needs an expander, and Spanish too. Could test. Creating nested subdecks and check both arrows + expansion nesting. Then delete.\n\nAlso, rotation with expanded state: rotate to landscape → does the arrow state/expansion persist? The deck list collapsed state is stored in collection config (per deck expanded). Rotation recreates activity; should keep. Could test.\n\nAlso test deck list when a subdeck has cards: parent count should aggregate and arrow should still exist. Hmm.\n\nAlso: after deleting a subdeck, arrow removed (verified).\n\nAnother possible bug: deck row click area vs arrow; arrow click expands. Verified.\n\nLet me test nested subdecks: create Spanish::temp, then temp::sub (create subdeck under temp). Check Spanish arrow and temp arrow. Then delete temp (which deletes children?) — deleting parent with subdeck may warn \"delete deck and its subdecks\". Cleaning up nested gets complex but doable.\n\nActually simpler: test rotation now with a subdeck expanded. Let me create Spanish::temp again, expand, rotate landscape, check state, rotate back, delete subdeck.\n\nBefore that, cancel tag dialog and go to deck list."}
