{"type": "thinking", "text": "After Check Database, testtag is gone — only \"verb\" remains. Data restored to precondition. \n\nNow, so far no bugs found. Hmm. Let me re-examine the three changed areas more carefully for subtle issues.\n\nArea 1: Deck list arrows.\nWe tested:\n- No subdecks: no arrows.\n- Spanish with one subdeck: arrow on Spanish only.\n- Expand/collapse works.\n- Delete last subdeck: arrow gone.\n- Rotation persists.\n\nPotential subtle bug: a deck with subdecks but the *arrow built from the deck list's children* — what about a deck whose subdeck name creates implicit parents? E.g., create \"Grammar::Verbs\" without creating \"Grammar\" first. Then both Grammar and Grammar::Verbs exist; Grammar has subdecks → arrow. Fine.\n\nWhat about the arrow's click target overlapping the deck row? The arrow is at x=63, row starts after. Clicking arrow expands (worked).\n\nWhat about parent deck counts when subdecks have cards? Parent count should include subdeck cards; we could test by moving a note to temp deck (deck counts). Not arrow-specific.\n\nPotential bug: the arrow shown for *filtered decks* or *deck with no cards but subdecks*? We had temp2 (0 cards) with no arrow; Spanish had 4 cards + 1 subdeck with arrow. What about a deck with 0 cards and 1 subdeck: arrow should show. Not tested. Eh.\n\nArea 2: Add note deck chooser initial deck.\nWe tested Add from FAB (current deck Spanish → Add Spanish), Add from long-press (Spanish → Spanish), Add from browser (current Spanish → Spanish), and after \"Decide by note type\"/back. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the actual seeded bug: the deck chooser's initial deck when opened from a NEW note after previously *editing* a note of another deck? E.g., edit French note (editor deck French), save, then add new note → should be Spanish (current) but may show French? Let's test:\n- Current deck Spanish (highlighted).\n- Go to browser all decks, tap \"bonjour\" (French) to edit; editor deck shows French.\n- Save (no changes? Save button maybe disabled if unchanged) or back. Then Add new note → deck should be Spanish (current choice). If it shows French (leftover from editing), that's the seeded \"initial deck from deck list current choice\" bug!\n\nThat's a plausible scenario: NoteEditor state leaks between edit and add sessions. Let's test carefully without changing data: open bonjour, don't modify (or modify then revert), press back (no changes → no discard prompt), then tap + Add.\n\nActually simpler: In browser (Spanish filter), swipe deck filter to All decks, open a French note, view it, back. Then Add. Also from deck list long-press French → Browse cards → open French note etc.\n\nLet me test:\n1. Exit tag dialog (Cancel).\n2. Browser deck filter → All decks.\n3. Tap bonjour → Edit note (deck French).\n4. Press back twice? It exits to browser.\n5. Tap browser Add button (which adds note from browser) → deck should be current deck (Spanish) if change works; if it shows French → bug.\n6. Or go deck list and +.\n\nExpected: \"initial deck loaded from deck list's current choice\" = current deck Spanish. So Add should show Spanish.\n\nLet's do this."}
