{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! After pressing Enter, it says \"No cards found in deck 'Spanish'\" again. So the deck filter is still Spanish, even after tapping \"Search all decks\" earlier. So the \"Search all decks\" button did NOT remove the deck filter. It may have just re-run the search while keeping the deck filter (or done nothing). That's a potential bug: the snackbar action \"Search all decks\" should search across all decks (in AnkiDroid, this button clears the deck filter and re-searches \"all decks\" — actually it \"searches all decks\" by adding `deck:*`? Hmm).\n\nLet me recall: AnkiDroid browser behavior: when a search has no results within the current deck filter, the snackbar says \"No cards found in deck 'X'\" with button \"Search all decks\". Pressing it removes the deck restriction (\"all decks\") and searches. That's the expected behavior.\n\nObserved: pressed \"Search all decks\" → list became empty, no results; then Enter re-ran and still \"No cards found in deck 'Spanish'\". So the deck filter wasn't cleared. This seems like a legit bug! But wait — maybe tapping the button triggered a search with all decks but the UI still showed Spanish because... The snackbar reappeared with 'Spanish', so filter definitely still Spanish.\n\nHold on. Is it possible that tapping element 9 (Search all decks) actually triggered something else? The snackbar action's clickable element was at (869,2190). I tapped element 9. The list went empty and the snackbar disappeared. Then Enter showed the same \"No cards found in deck 'Spanish'\" message. So the snackbar action did something (cleared the list?) but didn't search all decks.\n\nHmm, could it be that the list went empty because it re-ran the search *without* deck filter but with tag:ftag, and there were no results because... bonjour's tag ftag wasn't saved? Wait: did the tag actually attach to bonjour? We saved the note after Tags: ftag. The browser list still showed 7 cards. Let me verify the tag is on bonjour: reopen the note? Let me check via search \"tag:ftag\" after resetting the deck to All decks. If bonjour doesn't have ftag, then this explains the empty results and there's no bug in \"Search all decks\" — just the tag didn't save (or the note save didn't include tags?!).\n\nHmm! Let's check: after saving with \"Tags: ftag\", the browser list didn't show tags (it doesn't). Let me open bonjour and check its Tags button. But right now we're in search mode with Spanish filter. Collapse search → browser; then deck filter All decks; search tag:ftag; check.\n\nActually first: was the tag saved? When I saved, snackbar \"7 cards shown\" appeared; the note editor closed. The Tags button showed \"Tags: ftag\" before saving, so the note model had the tag. Save should persist. Unless... there's a bug where new tags typed via the \"+\" button don't get saved until...? Earlier testtag persisted (it appeared in the tag dialog after save, though that could be from the collection registration even if not on the note).\n\nWait, testtag: after we saved the note with testtag, we then deleted the note. So we never verified tag persistence on a note.\n\nHmm, this could be the seeded bug in \"adding and editing notes\": tags added in the tag dialog may not save? Let's verify bonjour's tags. Navigate: collapse search (36) then deck filter All decks then tap bonjour → Edit note → Tags button.\n\nLet's do it."}
