ks\" the list was empty and no snackbar. Then collapse → French 3. The deck filter was still French when collapsed. So the deck filter never changed. In the ftag case, Enter re-showed 'Spanish' snackbar. Reproduced twice.\n\nHmm, but maybe the button is *supposed* to switch the search to `deck:*` *without* changing the deck filter (search text becomes `(tag:ftag) deck:*`)? Then results should include bonjour. Empty → still bug.\n\nLet me look at what \"Search all decks\" should do based on AnkiDroid: In AnkiDroid's CardBrowser, there's `mSearchView` and a deck filter `mDeckId`. When a search has no results, the empty view shows a button \"Search all decks\" (id `search_all_decks`?). Clicking sets `mDeckId = ALL_DECKS_ID` and calls `searchCards()`. That's my memory from the source: `mEmptyView`... Actually I recall `mSearchView.setOnSearchClickListener` etc. There is a function `searchAllDecks()` maybe in `CardBrowser`: \n```\nprivate void searchAllDecks() {\n  mDeckId = Consts.ALL_DECKS_ID;\n  ...\n}\n```\nIf implemented correctly, results should appear.\n\nOK so I have a likely bug. But before reporting, let me also check whether the list being empty is just a UI refresh issue: after tapping \"Search all decks\", maybe the cards are loading asynchronously and the empty list persists due to a race. We waited ~3s; empty. Then Enter → snackbar 'Spanish'. Hmm.\n\nActually, hmm: maybe pressing \"Search all decks\" DID work but the search query became `comer` with deck filter All decks, and the list was empty because... the browser's \"selected deck\" still French and the result list... no, comer exists.\n\nLet me test the exact same flow but with a search that yields results in the *current* deck (e.g., French filter, search \"bonjour\") — sanity check that search works. Not needed.\n\nLet me try \"Search all decks\" again with the comer scenario and then check the deck selector label in search mode? The toolbar in search mode only shows query, not deck. After pressing the action, I can't see the deck filter until I collapse (which resets the search). Hmm.\n\nAlternative: after pressing \"Search all decks\", tap the overflow → \"Options\"? No.\n\nLet me try: after pressing \"Search all decks\" (empty list), rotate the device — maybe the list refreshes with results? If rotation shows comer, then the bug is a refresh issue, still a bug.\n\nHonestly, \"Search all decks\" failing to show cross-deck results is a real defect (either filter not cleared or results not refreshed). I should report it with exact steps and the snackbar quote. The element to point at: the snackbar action button \"Search all decks\" — element_ref from the latest observation at the time of the report. Currently in browser after collapse. I need to reproduce and then file at the point where the defect is visible (after tapping, empty list). But the observed_quote must be text on screen showing the defect. The empty list has no text... The snackbar \"No cards found in deck 'French'\" is shown before; the defect is that after tapping \"Search all decks\", results remain empty. A quote that was never on screen gets rejected. I can quote \"No cards found in deck ‘French’\" (was on screen) and maybe the query \"comer\". The observation after tapping showed query \"comer\" (in search field) and no rows. The quote could be \"comer\" — but that's not evidence. Hmm.\n\nMaybe better: the bug could be reported as \"Search all decks button has no effect\" (symptom_type no_effect), element_ref = the snackbar action button. Quote: \"No cards found in deck ‘French’\" — the message that offers the action. Reasonable.\n\nBut is this genuine? Let me first reproduce once more and observe the exact state after tapping: does the snackbar disappear and list remain empty? Yes.\n\nWait, actually maybe I'm misreading the current result: After tapping \"Search all decks\", the observation (8 elements) listed no card rows — but maybe the browser was still in \"search in progress\" state. The screenshot showed empty list with the cursor in search field. Also the \"Cards shown\" label isn't visible in search mode. Hmm.\n\nLet me test the equivalent in a different way: When browser is filtering French and I search \"comer\", the empty-result snackbar appears. Tap \"Search all decks\" — if the app switched to All decks,", "truncated": true}
