{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: after tapping \"Search all decks\", the deck filter is still French (\"No cards found in deck 'French'\"). So the action has no effect other than dismissing the snackbar.\n\nWait, actually is it possible that the action *did* switch to all decks but then the Enter search re-applied the old deck filter because the toolbar's selected deck is stored separately and the action only applied a temporary `deck:*` to the current query? If the query had `deck:*` appended, pressing Enter would re-submit \"comer\" + maybe `deck:*` from the field? The search field shows \"comer\" only. Hmm.\n\nLet me check the actual behavior in AnkiDroid: I recall the snackbar action in CardBrowser is implemented as:\n```\nmSearchAllDecksSnackbar.setAction(R.string.search_all_decks, v -> {\n    mDeckId = ALL_DECKS_ID;\n    mSearchView.setQuery(mSearchView.getQuery(), true);\n    ...\n});\n```\nIf so, it should work. Here it doesn't.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I'm wrong about the semantics: maybe \"Search all decks\" means to search for the *current query* across all decks *without changing the filter*, i.e., adding `deck:*` to the query. After tapping, the query should become \"(comer) deck:*\" visible in the field. It stayed \"comer\". So no effect.\n\nI'm fairly confident this is a bug. But is it within the sweep areas? Yes, card browser.\n\nHowever, I worry it might be a pre-existing stock behavior in this build that the developer won't consider a bug... but a QA finding is a finding. The instructions say file reports for bugs found in the areas. I'll report it.\n\nBefore that, let me double-check one alternative explanation: maybe the tap on element 9 at (869,2190) hit the snackbar but the action's callback requires the snackbar to not be dismissed... The snackbar disappeared, so the action was triggered. And the list became empty (refresh?) — that indicates the action ran a search but with the same filter, resulting in zero results and no snackbar? Odd: why no snackbar after re-search? Because the snackbar was dismissed by the tap and the re-search's snackbar maybe didn't show again? In earlier ftag case, after tapping, no snackbar; after Enter, snackbar appeared. So the re-search didn't show results.\n\nHmm, maybe the re-search is done with the deck filter *All decks* but a *search string* that includes `deck:\"French\"`? E.g., the browser builds the query with the deck prefix, and after the action sets mDeckId = ALL_DECKS_ID, it re-searches with the OLD full query \"deck:\\\"French\\\" comer\"? That would return 0 → empty list, and \"No cards found\" message would show... but the message checks if mDeckId != ALL_DECKS_ID, so with All decks it wouldn't show a snackbar → matches observed: empty list, no snackbar! Then pressing Enter re-searches — but why did the snackbar say 'French' again? Hmm, because the deck filter display in the toolbar is still French? The message 'No cards found in deck French' indicates mDeckId is French again.\n\nUnless pressing Enter (keyboard action) restores the deck filter from the toolbar's deck selector, which is still French (because the action didn't update the toolbar). Hmm.\n\nSo the underlying issue: the browser's deck filter isn't updated by the action, OR the search uses stale query. Either way, user-visible bug: tapping \"Search all decks\" yields an empty list instead of results.\n\nLet me also check: after tapping \"Search all decks\", maybe the deck filter selector in the toolbar changed only after the search is exited? When I collapsed, the toolbar showed French | 3 cards. But collapse might reset the deck filter to the pre-search value? I'm not sure. Let me test that explicitly: French filter, search comer, tap Search all decks, then instead of collapsing, open the drawer? No. Hmm, in search mode there's no deck selector. There's the \"More options\" but no deck.\n\nWait, maybe the snackbar action's intended effect is visible in the toolbar only after the snackbar action and before Enter — but in search mode the toolbar shows query, not deck. Hmm.\n\nAlternative check: the browser's \"cards shown\" count text when search is active is replaced by query. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at this from the source-knowledge perspective: In AnkiDroid CardBrowser, `mDeckId` is passed via the toolbar deck spinner. The \"no cards found in deck X\" message uses `mDeckName`. The SearchAllDecks action is in `mSearchView`'s `OnQueryTextListener`? I recall `CardBrowser.showSnackbar` with `R.string.search_all_decks` calling `onSearchAllDecks()`:\n```\nprivate void searchAllDecks() {\n    mDeckId = ALL_DECKS_ID;\n    String searchText = mSearchView.getQuery().toString();\n    mSearchView.setQuery(searchText, true);\n}\n```\nHmm. Would produce results.\n\nI'll report this as a bug. But first, let me test one more related browser behavior: after tapping \"Search all decks\", if I rotate the screen, does the list refresh with comer? If yes, it's a refresh bug; if no, filter not applied. Either way bug. Let's not overdo.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether the empty list after tapping might be because the search *did* switch to all decks and re-ran, but the app searched with a *stale* query that had the deck filter embedded (e.g., `deck:\"French\" comer`) — where did that come from? The search field showed \"comer\", so the query embedded isn't visible. The search might use `mSearchView.getQuery()` plus the deck filter stored. So after switching mDeckId to All, the query should be just \"comer\". Then results = comer. Not empty. So mDeckId probably didn't change.\n\nOK. Filing.\n\nWait, one more consideration: the reported defect might actually be *my* misuse: the \"Search all decks\" snackbar might exist to search *the current query* in all decks but requires *tapping the button quickly before the snackbar times out*? We tapped while visible. Fine.\n\nNow, before filing, let me also finish testing the changed tag dialog once more with the browser's *filter by tag* -> add tag via edit tags path: we've verified collection-wide and refresh. Good.\n\nAlso let me remember to clean up ftag from bonjour and check database to purge. I'll do that after filing.\n\nLet me now file the \"Search all decks\" bug. Element ref: current observation 9 = Button \"Search all decks\". The snackbar text quote: \"No cards found in deck ‘French’\". The defect visible: after tapping, list empty. I'll describe expected vs observed.\n\nActually, wait. I want to be sure the defect is \"no effect\" and not a legitimate behavior where the deck filter intentionally stays and the button just re-searches within the deck (weird). The button label \"Search all decks\" is unambiguous.\n\nHmm, but hold on: maybe the app intends the button to *set the search text* to include all decks, and the browser will show results after the async search completes — but our list is empty because of a **bug introduced by the tag-dialog refresh change**? No.\n\nHmm, maybe the issue is that the \"Search all decks\" action triggers a search on the **cards table** with the `where` args cached... Whatever, user-visible bug.\n\nLet me file it now.\n\nActually, wait! Before filing, let me consider the possibility that this is not a bug but a known behavior: In AnkiDroid, when you search within a deck and get no results, the snackbar has \"Search all decks\". I've used this feature; it definitely brings up matching cards from other decks. So yes, bug.\n\nLet me also test if pressing \"Search all decks\" when results exist (bonjour search) changes the toolbar to All decks after collapsing. Earlier after the bonjour search I didn't tap it. Let me test that variant because it may reveal the action's actual effect (it should switch to All decks and keep the search). If after tapping with results, the deck filter becomes All decks (count 7 when collapsed), then the action works in that case and the bug is only in the no-results case (maybe the action is only wired for the no-results empty-view button, while the snackbar action is a different handler). Let's test:\n- French filter, search bonjour, tap \"Search all decks\" (snackbar action), expect toolbar All decks after collapsing (or search remains bonjour 1 card).\n\nThen if that works, the no-results snackbar action still failing is a bug.\n\nLet me test. Cur", "truncated": true}
