ait, maybe in the no-results case, after tapping the action the deck filter became All decks AND the search re-ran, but the list showed empty because of a *refresh bug*. And then pressing Enter re-ran the search with the deck filter... hmm, why 'French'? Maybe because the browser's deck filter toolbar still had French and pressing Enter in the search field re-applies the *toolbar's* deck, which was not updated in the no-results path. But with results, collapsing showed All decks, so the toolbar *was* updated.\n\nHmm, this is getting confusing. Let me do a cleaner experiment in the no-results case and check the deck filter afterward by collapsing (instead of Enter):\n- French filter, search comer (0 results, snackbar).\n- Tap Search all decks.\n- Immediately collapse (tap the back arrow / Collapse) and check toolbar deck label.\n\nIf toolbar shows All decks → action changed filter but list failed to refresh (bug: empty list after action). If toolbar shows French → action didn't change filter (bug: no effect).\n\nAlso, the empty list after the action is itself the user-visible bug: after tapping \"Search all decks\", no cards appear.\n\nLet me do it. Currently All decks (post previous action), no search. Set deck filter French, search comer, tap action, then collapse, check.\n\nActually, I realize the empty list in the no-results case might just be because the search *did* switch to all decks and re-ran \"comer\"... but no results because the search text got mangled? The field still showed \"comer\". Hmm.\n\nLet me perform the clean experiment."}
