thout activating the action? The snackbar dismisses on tap outside/inside? If I tapped the snackbar background (not the button), it would dismiss silently, leaving the empty list (from the search) — and Enter re-runs the search in French → snackbar again. And in the successful cases, my tap hit the button.\n\nElement 9 was the Button \"Search all decks\" at (869,2190) with bounds... The tap tool taps the element center. Hmm, the button's element center should be the button. But maybe the button's actual clickable area is a bit off? The earlier tap at element 9 → snackbar disappeared without action. And now same element 9 → worked. Flaky hit-testing? The tap coordinates (869,2190) may be near the snackbar's edge? The snackbar spans 20..1060 x 2090..2270? The button at x~735-1005, y~2190. Center (869,2190) should be fine.\n\nHmm, why would it fail then work with identical procedure? Maybe difference: screen rotation? No. Maybe first time there was an *autocomplete dropdown* or keyboard overlay? The keyboard was open when I tapped element 9 (I had just typed with submit; the keyboard remains open). Tapping the snackbar action at y=2190 while the keyboard occupies y>1400 — wait! The keyboard is visible when the search field has focus. The snackbar is at y=2189, which would be **behind/above the keyboard**? Actually the snackbar in the screenshot was drawn above the keyboard area? In the screenshot c2fe..., the snackbar was at y~2182 (bottom of the 2400 screen), and the keyboard was NOT shown in that screenshot (it disappeared after search submit). Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait: In the screenshot c2fe..., the snackbar is at the very bottom above the nav bar — no keyboard. When I tapped element 9, did the search field lose focus (keyboard hidden after submit)? Yes.\n\nBut in the earlier failed attempts, maybe the keyboard was still up and the snackbar was positioned above the keyboard (at y~?) — the tap at (869,2190) would hit the keyboard's bottom row! Indeed: when the keyboard is shown (as in the observation with keys at y=1701..2194), tapping y=2190 x=869 would hit the keyboard key area (the emoticon/enter area), not the snackbar. Wait, but the observation element 9 \"Search all decks\" was at (869,2190) — if the keyboard were shown, the snackbar wouldn't be at 2190; the accessibility tree would show it above the keyboard. Hmm, the observations after Enter showed the full keyboard element list (44 elements) with keys up to y=2194, and the snackbar \"No cards found\" at (371,2189) — overlapping the keyboard space! That means the snackbar was rendered *behind/over* the keyboard? That seems odd.\n\nLook at the earlier observation after typing \"comer\" with submit: Elements were 10 (no keyboard!) with snackbar at 2189. So the keyboard was hidden after submit. Hmm, but in the observation right before tapping, the keyboard was hidden.\n\nWait, the sequence in the failed attempts: I did `type_text(..., submit:true)` → observation 10 elements (no keyboard) + snackbar. Then tapped element 9 → empty. Hmm.\n\nIn the successful attempt: same. Hmm.\n\nOK so flakiness might be inherent (async). Or maybe my earlier taps were actually on the *empty view* area and dismissed the snackbar? The snackbar action might be clicked through? Hmm.\n\nActually, wait: in the failed attempts, could the tap have *dismissed* the snackbar because the snackbar's action was temporarily disabled? Then no action. The empty list persisted. Then Enter re-searched with French → snackbar. That fits \"tap dismissed snackbar without action\". Then in this successful case, tap hit the action.\n\nBoth used element 9 from the latest observation, which should be precise. Hmm, but the element center (869,2190) — the snackbar action button's element might have bounds that include a larger area? The element itself is a Button; center is correct.\n\nHmm, maybe there's a real hit-testing bug: the snackbar's action button is only clickable in part of its bounds? Flaky. Let me try tapping the button at an offset (e.g., x=900, y=2200) vs element center. But we shouldn't report flaky if it was my error.\n\nLet me repeat the failed scenario a few times to see. Actually, the important thing: the \"Search all decks\" action works at least sometimes. So the earlier \"bug\" may be a flaky/UI issue rather than deterministic. Given uncertainty and risk of false positive, I should not report it yet. Let me test it a few more times.\n\nCurrently: search comer, results 1 card, snackbar \"1 card shown\" (no action). The deck filter is now All decks presumably. Collapse to verify. Then set French, search comer, tap \"Search all decks\" and see. Let me repeat 2-3 times.\n\nCollapse → toolbar."}
